# The compiler's line of the refusal starts with the header's path on the machine, so the
# message is a contains: line. On wasip2 and wasip3, where OpenSSL has the block cipher too, the
# message names it as well (test/messages/aes_block_default_not_linked_wasm); compile-diagnostic
# is clang's and skips Emscripten, so this fixture is the Emscripten one.
[all]
targets: emscripten
build: fails
# tag::messages[]
contains: webcpp::crypto: AES block cipher's default backend on this target is ctaes, which is not linked, and the one backend that has it there. Add /webcpp/crypto//aes_block-default, the default's library on every target, to the program's Jamfile, as in: exe app : app.cpp /webcpp/crypto//crypto /webcpp/crypto//aes_block-default ; (without b2: define WEBCPP_CRYPTO_HAS_CTAES=1 and link ctaes.c with webcpp's src/canary_ctaes.c)
# end::messages[]
